    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by [ a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "a rich silk brocade (OED s.v. baldachin, Heyd 686-7) | Canopies over such features as thrones, altars, tombs, or doorways; may be suspended, projecting, or free-standing.\" [Source: Getty AAT] | a rich embroidered stuff, originally woven with woof of silk and warp of gold thread; rich brocade. (OED s.v. baldachin, Heyd, 686-7) | Canopies over such features as thrones, altars, tombs, or doorways; may be suspended, projecting, or free-standing. [Source: Getty AAT]" ;
